Use bootstrap confidence intervals or Wilson confidence intervals for observed withdrawal rates by risk tier. Display sample sizes next to rates. Do not interpret a rate from fewer than 50 projects as a stable standard.

### Selection rule

Prefer the simplest model when its performance is close to the best challenger. A reasonable rule is to retain logistic regression unless another model improves chronological ROC-AUC by at least 0.02 **and** improves or preserves Brier score and calibration. Explain the final selection in plain language.

